ence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Rich McCormick (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Georgia's 7th District, in Atlanta's northern suburbs, leans Republican by about 11 points. Incumbent Rich McCormick has raised $2.25 million, more than double Democrat Tony Kozycki's $922,000, and enters November with a large cash advantage. Expert raters unanimously place the race in the Republican column, most calling it Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Kozycki roughly a 9 percent chance of winning.\n\nThere are some signs of Democratic energy. A Democratic-leaning pollster's October survey showed the race essentially tied, and this year's national environment appears several points friendlier to Democrats than the district's usual margin. Sen. Jon Ossoff has endorsed Kozycki, and turnout activity in the north metro area is active. Even so, the district's lean, incumbency, and fundraising gap make McCormick a clear favorite, with Kozycki needing an unusually strong wave to close the distance.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0501, "margin": -12.18}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1218, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0672, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0801, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0796, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0786, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0751, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0581, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0723, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0639, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0756, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1071, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1041, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0789, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.027, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0454, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0486, "mar